# Final Report Placeholder

## 📄 Project Report

The final project report (PDF) will be placed here after completion.

### Report Structure

The report should include the following sections:

#### 1. Cover Page
- Project title
- Student name
- Course information
- Date
- Institution

#### 2. Executive Summary (1 page)
- Brief project overview
- Key findings
- Main achievements

#### 3. Introduction (1-2 pages)
- Problem statement
- Domain selection rationale
- Project objectives
- Scope and limitations

#### 4. Literature Review (1 page)
- LoRA methodology
- Related work in medical NLP
- Parameter-efficient fine-tuning

#### 5. Methodology (2-3 pages)
- **Dataset:**
  - Source and description
  - Preprocessing pipeline
  - Statistics and analysis
  
- **Model Architecture:**
  - Base model selection
  - LoRA configuration
  - Memory optimization techniques
  
- **Training:**
  - Hyperparameter configurations
  - Experiment design
  - Training infrastructure

#### 6. Experiments & Results (2-3 pages)
- **Experiment Table:**
  - All 4 experiments with hyperparameters
  - Training and evaluation metrics
  
- **Quantitative Results:**
  - BLEU, ROUGE, Perplexity scores
  - Comparison with baseline
  - Statistical significance
  
- **Qualitative Analysis:**
  - Sample responses
  - Medical accuracy improvements
  - Error analysis

#### 7. Deployment (1 page)
- Gradio interface design
- User interaction flow
- Accessibility features

#### 8. Discussion (1-2 pages)
- Key findings and insights
- Impact of hyperparameters
- Challenges and solutions
- Comparison with expectations

#### 9. Conclusion & Future Work (1 page)
- Summary of achievements
- Contributions
- Limitations
- Future improvements

#### 10. References
- All citations (LoRA paper, TinyLlama, datasets, etc.)

#### 11. Appendices
- **Appendix A:** Code snippets (key functions)
- **Appendix B:** Additional experiment results
- **Appendix C:** Full experiment data tables

### Required Links in Report

Make sure to include:
- ✅ GitHub repository link
- ✅ Colab notebook link (with badge)
- ✅ Demo video link
- ✅ Dataset source link

### Formatting Guidelines

- **Length:** 7-10 pages (excluding appendices)
- **Font:** Times New Roman or Arial, 11-12pt
- **Spacing:** 1.5 or double-spaced
- **Margins:** 1 inch all sides
- **Citations:** IEEE or APA format
- **Figures:** High-quality, with captions and labels
- **Tables:** Clear formatting, proper headers

### Figures to Include

1. Dataset statistics (length distribution)
2. Model architecture diagram (LoRA visualization)
3. Experiment results comparison chart
4. Evaluation metrics comparison (bar chart)
5. Sample conversation screenshots
6. Gradio interface screenshot

### Tables to Include

1. Experiment configurations table
2. Results summary table
3. Baseline vs fine-tuned comparison
4. Dataset preprocessing statistics

### Submission Checklist

Before submitting the report:
- [ ] Spell-check and grammar check
- [ ] All figures have captions
- [ ] All tables have headers
- [ ] All links are working
- [ ] Code snippets are formatted
- [ ] References are complete
- [ ] Page numbers added
- [ ] Table of contents (if required)
- [ ] PDF file size < 10MB
- [ ] File named appropriately: `StudentName_MedicalLLM_Report.pdf`

